# civil-holidays v1
# jurisdiction: GR
# source: https://www.gov.gr/arxes/upourgeio-ergasias-kai-koinonikes-asphaliseis
#   (Greek statutory public holidays / υποχρεωτικές αργίες — Ν. 4808/2021 art. 60
#   and Β.Δ. 748/1966, as codified. Local copy papers/holidays/gr_holidays.md.)
#   ORTHODOX EASTER: Greece reckons Easter on the Orthodox (Julian-computus)
#   calendar, so every Easter-relative holiday uses method julian_gregorian_date,
#   NOT the Western computus. In 2024 Orthodox Easter is 5 May, whence Καθαρά
#   Δευτέρα (Clean Monday, −48) = 18 Mar, Μεγάλη Παρασκευή (Good Friday, −2) =
#   3 May, Δευτέρα του Πάσχα (Easter Monday, +1) = 6 May, Δευτέρα του Αγίου
#   Πνεύματος (Holy Spirit / Whit Monday, +50) = 24 Jun — the Orthodox reckoning
#   flowing straight through the computus. Names are the official Greek.
# retrieved: 2026-07-21
# categories: public|regional|municipal|religious|school
# columns: kind | name | args | categories | subdiv | observed
#
fixed   | Πρωτοχρονιά                        | 1 1                    | public          |  |
fixed   | Θεοφάνεια                          | 1 6                    | public religious |  |
easter  | Καθαρά Δευτέρα                     | -48 julian_gregorian_date | public religious |  |
